WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:07.663
"Go, Luke!"

2
00:00:15.128 --> 00:00:15.888
cheered Katie.

3
00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:19.190
She was waving the ribbon wand she had just made.

4
00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.092
Luke was stomping across the room on stilts.

5
00:00:23.672 --> 00:00:25.473
He was practicing for the parade.

6
00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:28.315
"Left, right, left, right!"

7
00:00:28.635 --> 00:00:29.335
directed Mrs.

8
00:00:31.252 --> 00:00:32.233
Penkov. "Be careful!"

9
00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:33.434
called AJ.

10
00:00:34.835 --> 00:00:40.158
Campers beat on their drums, shook their shakers, and twirled their twirlers.

11
00:00:41.319 --> 00:00:43.440
Today was day five of camp.

12
00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:50.365
Saturday was Willow Creek's birthday, and the campers were almost ready for the parade.

13
00:00:51.526 --> 00:00:54.148
But time was running out for the scavenger hunt.

14
00:00:55.269 --> 00:01:00.092
In less than two days, they had to turn in their bags—ready or not.

15
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.823
That afternoon the Earthworms gathered at Fried Pie Heaven.

16
00:01:06.904 --> 00:01:09.326
Katie took a bite of peach fried pie.

17
00:01:09.346 --> 00:01:12.489
"Luke's getting his hair cut," she said.

18
00:01:12.509 --> 00:01:13.750
"He'll be late."

19
00:01:14.871 --> 00:01:18.694
"You're not supposed to talk with food in your mouth," said AJ.

20
00:01:20.055 --> 00:01:21.376
Katie took another bite.

21
00:01:21.396 --> 00:01:26.080
"I'll remember that next time," she said with her mouth full.

22
00:01:27.301 --> 00:01:30.664
Emily was checking the scavenger hunt list one more time.

23
00:01:31.828 --> 00:01:35.591
"We're lucky my dad had that old campaign button," she said.

24
00:01:35.611 --> 00:01:43.438
"Now the only thing we're missing is—" Just then Luke ran into the coffee shop.

25
00:01:43.458 --> 00:01:46.621
"Guess what I learned at the barber shop!"

26
00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:47.421
he said.

27
00:01:47.982 --> 00:01:49.623
Luke sat down at the table.

28
00:01:49.643 --> 00:01:56.149
"No one in Willow Creek is allowed to own a dog that barks too loud or too often!"

29
00:01:56.169 --> 00:01:59.612
"So?" said AJ.

30
00:02:00.764 --> 00:02:01.964
"So it's a law!"

31
00:02:02.445 --> 00:02:03.065
said Luke.

32
00:02:03.085 --> 00:02:05.605
"A Willow Creek law!"

33
00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:09.306
said Emily, waving the scavenger list in the air.

34
00:02:09.326 --> 00:02:12.167
"Do you know what this means, team?"

35
00:02:12.187 --> 00:02:15.308
"We're almost finished with the hunt!"

36
00:02:15.868 --> 00:02:16.588
said Katie.

37
00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:23.210
Down the street at the library, the Tornadoes were checking their list too.

38
00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.571
"Where's the note from Mr.

39
00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:27.231
Potter?" asked Laura.

40
00:02:27.251 --> 00:02:30.460
"It's right here," said Carlos.

41
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.621
"Milton Christopher Potter.

42
00:02:33.121 --> 00:02:34.621
Ninety-seven years old."

43
00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.042
Now everyone turned to Manny.

44
00:02:38.062 --> 00:02:42.023
"Manny," said Joy with her grown-up voice.

45
00:02:42.043 --> 00:02:46.505
"We are depending on your outstanding counting skills.

46
00:02:46.985 --> 00:02:48.165
Are you ready to report?"

47
00:02:49.986 --> 00:02:52.486
"Yes, I am," said Manny.

48
00:02:52.506 --> 00:02:54.907
"Okay," said Joy.

49
00:02:54.927 --> 00:02:58.768
"How many stop signs did you count on Main Street?"

50
00:03:00.096 --> 00:03:01.837
"Seven," said Manny.

51
00:03:01.857 --> 00:03:05.600
"Mailboxes?" "Two."

52
00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:10.123
"And last how many streetlamps did you count?"

53
00:03:11.384 --> 00:03:15.507
"Eighteen." Laura looked up from the list.

54
00:03:16.107 --> 00:03:19.950
"We're done with the hunt!"

55
00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.291
"Hooray!" cheered the Tornadoes.

56
00:03:22.311 --> 00:03:25.013
"Shh!" said Mrs.

57
00:03:25.073 --> 00:03:28.516
Donovan. "Use your library voices, please!"

58
00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:30.821
"We're going to win!"

59
00:03:31.361 --> 00:03:32.262
whispered Joy.

60
00:03:34.123 --> 00:03:36.164
Friday was the last day of camp.

61
00:03:36.184 --> 00:03:38.746
"Teams!" said Mrs.

62
00:03:38.806 --> 00:03:41.448
Penkov. "Are you ready to turn in your bags?"

63
00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:44.250
"The Earthworms are ready!"

64
00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:45.551
called AJ.

65
00:03:46.652 --> 00:03:49.654
He grabbed the team bag and carried it up to Mrs.

66
00:03:49.714 --> 00:03:53.576
Penkov. "It's the marble lady!"

67
00:03:54.117 --> 00:03:56.458
squeaked Manny as AJ passed by.

68
00:03:56.478 --> 00:03:58.940
The Earthworms' jaws dropped.

69
00:03:59.924 --> 00:04:01.786
"What? That was YOU?"

70
00:04:02.566 --> 00:04:03.547
sputtered Katie.

71
00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:06.089
She shook her fist.

72
00:04:06.589 --> 00:04:08.410
The Tornadoes burst out laughing.

73
00:04:11.352 --> 00:04:13.714
The other teams carried their bags to Mrs.

74
00:04:13.774 --> 00:04:23.501
Penkov. She arranged them in a row on the table: Airplanes, Lizards, Watermelons, Earthworms, Tornadoes.

75
00:04:23.521 --> 00:04:26.143
"When will you announce the winner?"

76
00:04:26.623 --> 00:04:27.324
asked Joy.

77
00:04:28.508 --> 00:04:30.429
"After the parade," said Mrs.

78
00:04:30.489 --> 00:04:35.151
Penkov. "And then you'll give out the prizes, right?"

79
00:04:35.571 --> 00:04:36.252
said Katie.

80
00:04:36.272 --> 00:04:39.133
"Of course," said Mrs.

81
00:04:39.193 --> 00:04:44.135
Penkov. "And since you have worked so hard, I think you all deserve a prize."

82
00:04:45.356 --> 00:04:47.837
She pulled a big box from under the table.

83
00:04:47.857 --> 00:04:50.698
"Surprise!" she cried.

84
00:04:50.718 --> 00:04:54.180
"HAPPY BIRTHDAY WILLOW CREEK T-shirts!"

85
00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.230
The day campers clapped and cheered.

86
00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:02.434
"T-shirts for everyone!"

87
00:05:02.954 --> 00:05:06.297
Mrs. Penkov laughed and tossed T-shirts right and left.

88
00:05:06.317 --> 00:05:08.939
"Yellow for the Airplanes.

89
00:05:09.419 --> 00:05:10.821
Blue for the Tornadoes.

90
00:05:11.281 --> 00:05:12.562
Green for the Lizards.

91
00:05:13.763 --> 00:05:15.084
Red for the Watermelons.

92
00:05:15.484 --> 00:05:17.226
And orange for the Earthworms."

93
00:05:17.246 --> 00:05:19.848
"Thank you, Mrs.

94
00:05:19.908 --> 00:05:22.450
Penkov!" shouted the campers.

95
00:05:23.671 --> 00:05:25.452
"You're welcome," said Mrs.

96
00:05:25.532 --> 00:05:28.034
Penkov. "But—we still have work to do!

97
00:05:29.114 --> 00:05:31.235
The marchers can help me finish our banner.

98
00:05:32.356 --> 00:05:34.377
The riders can decorate their bikes.

99
00:05:35.597 --> 00:05:38.359
And Luke, get up on those stilts and practice!

100
00:05:38.799 --> 00:05:40.420
Tomorrow is the big day!"
